{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.a167f8e2be","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-1","passage":"<p>The museum announced that ______ plan for the summer included several community events.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["it's","their","its","they're"],"answer":"C","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the museum,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.a0e886b670","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-1","passage":"<p>The museum announced that ______ decision surprised many observers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["their","they're","it's","its"],"answer":"D","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the museum,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.0fb6383e77","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-4","passage":"<p>The library announced that ______ goals for the year were ambitious.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["it's","their","they're","its"],"answer":"D","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the library,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.dd49e79f70","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_tense","group":"tense-1","passage":"<p>So far this year, the museum ______ several rare paintings.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["acquired","will acquire","had acquired","has acquired"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The verb tense must fit the time frame of the sentence, which is set by “So far this year,” a period that continues up to the present, so the present perfect (“has” plus the past participle) is needed. The correct choice is “has acquired.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.dde6454408","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_tense","group":"tense-5","passage":"<p>So far this year, the farm ______ hundreds of apple trees.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["had planted","planted","has planted","will plant"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The verb tense must fit the time frame of the sentence, which is set by “So far this year,” a period that continues up to the present, so the present perfect (“has” plus the past participle) is needed. The correct choice is “has planted.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.987bf35f0b","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_tense","group":"tense-6","passage":"<p>So far this year, the author ______ four novels.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["published","had published","has published","will publish"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The verb tense must fit the time frame of the sentence, which is set by “So far this year,” a period that continues up to the present, so the present perfect (“has” plus the past participle) is needed. The correct choice is “has published.”"}
